# Project Alexandria — .gitignore
#
# Controls what ships in the open-source release. The principle is simple:
# the notes are the artifact, everything below is per-machine state, course
# material, or OS junk that has no business in a public repository.
#
# What is intentionally NOT ignored, and why:
#   - .obsidian/app.json, appearance.json, hotkeys.json, types.json,
#     core-plugins.json, community-plugins.json — define the portable vault
#     configuration so a stranger cloning the repo gets the same setup.
#   - .obsidian/snippets/ and .obsidian/themes/ — user-authored CSS that
#     belongs to the vault.
#   - .obsidian/plugins/<plugin>/main.js, manifest.json, styles.css — the
#     compiled plugin code (so cloners don't have to reinstall every plugin).
#   - attachments/ — images and files referenced from notes.
#   - CLAUDE.md, README.md — vault standards.
#
# Whitelist-style entries (the `!pattern` lines) live in the .obsidian
# section. They re-allow specific files that the broad `.obsidian/*` rule
# above would otherwise ignore.

# ============================================================
# Course materials (private)
# ============================================================
# Lecture slides, problem sets, textbook chapters, and other Berkeley course
# artifacts that seed the notes but are not redistributed. See
# _sources/README.md for the full provenance and copyright policy.
_sources/

# ============================================================
# Obsidian per-machine state (whitelist approach)
# ============================================================
# Ignore everything in .obsidian/ by default, then re-allow the specific
# files that define portable vault configuration. This protects against
# future Obsidian releases adding new files that may contain machine-
# specific paths or personal data.
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json
!.obsidian/appearance.json
!.obsidian/core-plugins.json
!.obsidian/community-plugins.json
!.obsidian/hotkeys.json
!.obsidian/types.json
!.obsidian/graph.json
!.obsidian/snippets/
!.obsidian/themes/
!.obsidian/plugins/

# Within plugins, ignore per-user data and caches but keep compiled code
# (main.js, manifest.json, styles.css).
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data-*.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/.cache/

# Workspace files contain window layouts and recently-opened paths.
# Listed explicitly because some Obsidian versions write variants the
# whitelist would otherwise let through.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspace.json.bak

# ============================================================
# MakeMD per-machine state
# ============================================================
# View definitions, filter caches, and per-folder frontmatter overrides.
# These pollute the graph view (see Vault Note-by-Note Analysis §III) and
# don't survive cleanly across machines.
.makemd/
.space/
**/.space/

# ============================================================
# Obsidian trash
# ============================================================
# .trash/ is temporary by policy (README §6); never ship it publicly. Git
# history is the long-term record, not .trash.
.trash/

# ============================================================
# Scratch and working state
# ============================================================
_scratch/

# ============================================================
# macOS
# ============================================================
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.fuse_hidden*
.VolumeIcon.icns
Icon
Icon?
._*

# ============================================================
# Windows
# ============================================================
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ============================================================
# Linux
# ============================================================
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ============================================================
# Editors and IDEs
# ============================================================
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.netrwhist
.project
.settings/

# ============================================================
# Office and LibreOffice lock and temp files
# ============================================================
# These appear when a .docx is open in Word or LibreOffice and prevent
# concurrent edits. They have no business in version control.
~$*
.~lock.*#

# ============================================================
# Generic temp / backup / log files
# ============================================================
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.obsidian/
